<setup><copy source="$x1" link="false" name="ref1" /><copy source="$y1" link="false" name="ref2" /><copy source="$x2" link="false" name="ref3" /><copy source="$y2" link="false" name="ref4" /><copy source="$x3" link="false" name="ref5" /><copy source="$y3" link="false" name="ref6" /><copy source="$x1" link="false" name="ref7" /><copy source="$y4" link="false" name="ref8" /><copy source="$x2" link="false" name="ref9" /><copy source="$y1" link="false" name="ref10" /><copy source="$x3" link="false" name="ref11" /><copy source="$y2" link="false" name="ref12" /><copy source="$x3" link="false" name="ref13" /><copy source="$y4" link="false" name="ref14" /><copy source="$x1" link="false" name="ref15" /><copy source="$y3" link="false" name="ref16" /><copy source="$x2" link="false" name="ref17" /><copy source="$y4" link="false" name="ref18" /><copy source="$x3" link="false" name="ref19" /><copy source="$y1" link="false" name="ref20" /><copy source="$x1" link="false" name="ref21" /><copy source="$y2" link="false" name="ref22" /><copy source="$x2" link="false" name="ref23" /><copy source="$y3" link="false" name="ref24" /></setup><!--************************************************************
Author: University of Minnesota PreCalculus Dept.
Reviewed/Remixed by: Doenet team

About the problem: Given a set of mathematical statements, sort them into their appropriate category of inequality, expression, or equation
*************************************************************-->

<problem>

<setup>
  <select assignNames="x1 x2 x3" numToSelect="3">-6.8 0 6.8</select>
  <select assignNames="y1 y2 y3 y4" numToSelect="4">6.5 7.5 8.5 9.5</select>
  <selectFromSequence assignNames="a b c d e" numToSelect="5" from="1" to="10" />

  <math name="eq1" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref1, $ref2)">$a x + $b x^2 = $e</math>
  <math name="eq2" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref3, $ref4)">$d - y = 2 $a</math>
  <math name="eq3" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref5, $ref6)">sqrt($b z) = $a^2</math>
  <math name="eq4" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref7, $ref8)">$a $b t = -s^2</math>

  <math name="expr1" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref9, $ref10)">-$a $e x - 2 $d y</math>
  <math name="expr2" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref11, $ref12)">1/z + $d z^2</math>
  <math name="expr3" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref13, $ref14)">sqrt($a) + y^2</math>
  <math name="expr4" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref15, $ref16)">-$c x y^2</math>

  <math name="ineq1" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref17, $ref18)">$e^2 /3 &lt;= $a + x</math>
  <math name="ineq2" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref19, $ref20)">x > $d/y</math>
  <math name="ineq3" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref21, $ref22)">-$b x - $d &lt; $a</math>
  <math name="ineq4" simplify="numberspreserveorder" anchor="($ref23, $ref24)">sqrt($b) &lt; t &lt; $b^2</math>
</setup>


<!--testing-->
<!-- <p>eq1.anchor = $eq1.anchor</p>
<p>eq2.anchor = $eq2.anchor</p>
<p>eq3.anchor = $eq3.anchor</p>
<p>eq4.anchor = $eq4.anchor</p>
<p>eqsCorrect = $eqsCorrect</p>

<p>expr1.anchor = $expr1.anchor</p>
<p>expr2.anchor = $expr2.anchor</p>
<p>expr3.anchor = $expr3.anchor</p>
<p>expr4.anchor = $expr4.anchor</p>
<p>exprsCorrect = $exprsCorrect</p>

<p>ineq1.anchor = $ineq1.anchor</p>
<p>ineq2.anchor = $ineq2.anchor</p>
<p>ineq3.anchor = $ineq3.anchor</p>
<p>ineq4.anchor = $ineq4.anchor</p>
<p>ineqsCorrect = $ineqsCorrect</p> -->
<!--testing-->

<!--*********************************************
           Problem Statement
**********************************************-->
<p>Sort each statement in the chart into its correct description, determining whether it is an <term>Inequality</term>, <term>Expression</term>, or <term>Equation</term>.</p>

<graph displayXAxis="false" displayYAxis="false" showNavigation="false">
  $eq1 $eq2 $eq3 $eq4 
  $expr1 $expr2 $expr3 $expr4
  $ineq1 $ineq2 $ineq3 $ineq4
  <rectangle fixed="true" styleNumber="5" vertices="(-20, 6) (20, 20)" />
  <lineSegment fixed="true" styleNumber="5" endpoints="(-10/3, -20) (-10/3, 6)" />
  <lineSegment fixed="true" styleNumber="5" endpoints="(10/3, -20) (10/3, 6)" />
  <label anchor="(-6.8, -9)" fixed="true"><m>\large{\text{Inequalities}}</m></label>
  <label anchor="(0, -9)" fixed="true"><m>\large{\text{Expressions}}</m></label>
  <label anchor="(6.8, -9)" fixed="true"><m>\large{\text{Equations}}</m></label>
</graph>

  
<!--*********************************************
            Solution input
**********************************************-->
<answer name="ans1">
    <award><when>$eq1.anchor.x > 10/3 and $eq2.anchor.x > 10/3 and
    $eq3.anchor.x > 10/3 and $eq4.anchor.x > 10/3 and $ineq1.anchor.x &lt; -10/3 and $ineq2.anchor.x &lt; -10/3 and
    $ineq3.anchor.x &lt; -10/3 and $ineq4.anchor.x &lt; -10/3 and $expr1.anchor.x &lt; 10/3 and $expr1.anchor.x > -10/3 and
    $expr2.anchor.x &lt; 10/3 and $expr2.anchor.x > -10/3 and
    $expr3.anchor.x &lt; 10/3 and $expr3.anchor.x > -10/3 and
    $expr4.anchor.x &lt; 10/3 and $expr4.anchor.x > -10/3</when>
    </award>
</answer>
  
<!--*********************************************
            Feedbacks
**********************************************-->
<setup>
  <select name="correctFeedback" type="text">
    <option>Awesome!</option>
    <option>Great job!</option>
    <option>Fantastic!</option>
    <option>Nice work!</option>
    <option>Amazing!</option>
    <option>Excellent!</option>
    <option>Right on!</option>
    <option>Perfect!</option>
  </select>
</setup>
  <feedback condition="$ans1.creditAchieved = 1">$correctFeedback</feedback>


<!--*********************************************
            Solution
**********************************************-->
<solution>
<p><alert>Inequalities</alert>: $ineq1, $ineq2, $ineq3, $ineq4</p>
<p><alert>Expressions</alert>: $expr1, $expr2, $expr3, $expr4</p>
<p><alert>Inequalities</alert>: $eq1, $eq2, $eq3, $eq4</p>
</solution>
</problem>






